---
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { showPlaceholderTags } from '../data/site';
const removed = ['Proposals', 'Status meetings', 'Pitch presentations', 'Design-to-dev handoffs', 'Account-manager relays', 'Repetitive setup', 'Manual research', 'Feedback by email chain'];
const kept = [
  { t: 'Senior creative direction', d: 'Every site is directed and signed off by a senior designer. Not reviewed. Directed.' },
  { t: 'Design and build together', d: 'We design in the medium it ships in. What you approve is what goes live.' },
  { t: 'A production system', d: 'Tested components, QA checklists and internal tooling handle the parts that should never be creative.' },
  { t: 'Thinking before pixels', d: 'Positioning, structure and copy come first. Pretty comes second, and only because it’s easier then.' },
];
const notThis = ['Templates', '$500 websites', 'Generic AI sites', 'Cookie-cutter layouts', 'Stock-photo heroes'];
---

<section class="py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-20">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="label text-spark">How it’s this fast</p>
        <h2 class="display mt-4 t-h2">Fast doesn’t mean rushed. <span class="accent text-spark">Fast means systematic.</span></h2>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-lg text-[18px] text-paper/65">
          Most of an agency timeline isn’t design or code. It’s waiting for the next meeting. We took that out and kept every hour of actual craft.
          The quality comes from creative decisions. The speed comes from the system around them.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-[16px] text-paper/45">Yes, there’s automation behind the curtain. No, it doesn’t design your website. It does the setup and the legwork so people can focus on the decisions that matter.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-[28px] bg-pine-800" data-reveal>
        <img src={url('/placeholder/team-laptops.webp')} alt="Team working on laptops (placeholder image)" loading="lazy" class="h-full min-h-[340px] w-full object-cover opacity-90" />
        {showPlaceholderTags && <span class="placeholder-tag absolute left-4 top-4">Placeholder</span>}
        <div class="absolute inset-x-4 bottom-4 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-pine-900/85 p-5 backdrop-blur-md">
          <p class="label text-paper/45">Removed from the process</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            {removed.map((r) => <li class="rounded-full border border-white/10 px-3 py-1 text-[13px] text-paper/60 line-through decoration-booked/70">{r}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-[28px] border border-white/10 bg-white/10 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      {kept.map((k, i) => (
        <div class="bg-pine-900 p-7" data-reveal>
          <p class="font-mono text-[13px] text-spark">0{i + 1}</p>
          <h3 class="mt-6 text-[20px] font-medium tracking-tight">{k.t}</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-paper/60">{k.d}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <!-- Quality positioning -->
    <div class="mt-24 rounded-[32px] bg-paper p-8 text-ink sm:p-14" data-reveal>
      <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.3fr_1fr] lg:items-end">
        <h2 class="display t-big">Built fast.<br /><span class="accent">Not made cheap.</span></h2>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[18px] text-ink/70">We’re not the cheapest way to get a website, and we don’t want to be. We’re the alternative to a $15–30K agency project that takes a quarter, without the parts of it you didn’t enjoy.</p>
          <p class="label mt-8 text-ink/45">What you won’t get</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            {notThis.map((n) => <li class="rounded-full border border-ink/15 px-3 py-1.5 text-[14px] text-ink/55 line-through">{n}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
